<Doc slug="updates">
  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <li>From Google Play, update Zafe as usual. When an update is ready inside the app, Home shows <strong>Update ready</strong>: tap it to restart. It waits while a payment is sending.</li>
    <li>Installed the APK? Install the newest one from <a href="/download">the download page</a> over the old one. Your vaults stay.</li>
    <li>Tell the others. Every member of a vault should be on a current version.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>NU7 on November 5</h2>
  <p>
    Zcash’s NU7 network upgrade activates on mainnet around November 5, 2026 (block
    3,543,405). Zafe 0.1.18 and newer are ready for it. Older versions can’t send after the
    upgrade. Funds are never at risk, but every member has to update before then.
  </p>
  <p>
    A payment proposed in the days before the upgrade gets a shorter approval window: it
    expires before the upgrade. If it doesn’t make it, propose it again afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2>If it goes wrong</h2>
  <dl class="doc-fixes">
    <div><dt>“Update Zafe”: other members use a newer version</dt><dd>Some vault activity only shows after you update. Update, then open the vault again.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>“<em>Name</em> must update Zafe first”</dt><dd>Shown on the Server screen before a move. That member updates; then the move is available.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>“The server needs an update”</dt><dd>The vault’s server is older than the app. Ask whoever runs it to update it, or <a href="/docs/move-servers">move to another server</a>.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</Doc>
